**Question:** How should a data row be handled when its cell count does not match the seven header columns (for example, six or eight cells)?

Why it matters: FR-003 requires every data row to receive exactly one classification, but no current rejection reason covers a row whose shape is malformed.

**Recommended:** Option B - rejecting any width mismatch prevents malformed rows from ever being partially imported, and it reuses an existing reason without inventing a new one.

| Option | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| A | Pad missing trailing cells with blanks and ignore cells beyond the seventh, then apply the normal validation precedence. |
| B | Treat any width mismatch as `missing_required_field`; never import a row whose width differs from the header. |
| C | Treat any width mismatch as `empty_row`. |
| Short | Provide a different short answer (<=5 words). |

You can reply with the option letter (e.g., "B"), accept the recommendation by saying "yes" or "recommended", or provide your own short answer.

